Upstream-bound: no
Subject: [PORT_HOST] P7.9 battle menu memory: the command menu and the technique list open on the last pick

The player's turn (FIGHTSTG_updatePlayerTurn) resets PlayerTurn.command to
Attack whenever it goes back to substate 0, and the command menu opens its
cursor on that value (FIGHTSTG_createCommandMenu(start)); the technique menu
always opens on the first technique of the first page. With the file-only key
`battle_menu_memory` in port_options.cfg (port/battle_menu/battle_menu_memory.c)
the port changes what those two starts are:

* the reset takes the command remembered (dw3_port_battle_menu_start_command),
  and every pick in the command menu is reported
  (dw3_port_battle_menu_command_picked: Attack, Techniques, Switch, Items;
  not Run, which ends the turn, nor Digivolve, which is greyed out for the
  form it leads to);
* the command menu opens on that value, or on Attack when the line is greyed
  out for the active fighter (asleep: Attack / Techniques / Digivolve;
  FIGHTER_NO_DIGIVOLVE: Digivolve), the cursor's start being the only thing
  that changes (dw3_port_battle_menu_open_command);
* with value 2 the technique menu puts its cursor on the technique this
  partner picked last (per party member), turning to its page, unless the
  list no longer has it or the fighter lacks the MP for it. Only the page,
  the cursor's line count and its line are set before the first
  FIGHTSTG_showTechPage; the picks, MP and the action are the menu's own.

Test hook (PORT_HOST, environment, no-op when unset): DW3_EXTRA_TECHS=<id>,<id>,...
adds techniques to the partner's list so the replay scenarios can look at
several lines and a second page; the stock Kotemon starts with Hot Head only.

With the key absent or 0 (the default) every hook returns the original value
(Attack, the command passed in, the first line), so the game state, the RNG
and the frames are bit-identical to a build without the patch. The memory
lives for the session only and is not part of any save. Same code on the US
and EU discs.

--- a/src/battle/battle_mode/player_turn.c
+++ b/src/battle/battle_mode/player_turn.c
@@ -2,6 +2,9 @@
    turn's action is picked. */
 
